  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12-2000-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x \\lt 2,\\) we have \\(|x - 2| = 2 - x = p,\\) so \\(x = 2 - p.\\)\n\nThen \\[ x - p = (2 - p) - p = 2 - 2p. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Since \\(x \\lt 2,\\) the quantity \\(x - 2\\) is negative, so \\(|x - 2| = 2 - x\\)",
        "Solve \\(2 - x = p\\) for \\(x,\\) then compute \\(x - p\\)"
      ],
